# Jago Akademi — automated Postgres backup (TASK-021).
# Install on host:  sudo cp deploy/jago-backup.cron /etc/cron.d/jago-backup
# Requires: docker compose stack up; (optional) rclone remote "r2" for offsite.
#
# Daily at 02:15 server time. Logs to /var/log/jago-backup.log.
#
# R2_REMOTE was shipped EMPTY here, which meant every backup landed only in
# /var/www/jago-akademi/backups — on the same VPS as the database it is meant to
# protect. Host loss = database and every backup gone together. RUNBOOK_DB.md
# documented r2:jago-backups but the installable artifact contradicted it, so the
# offsite copy was never actually enabled on any host.
#
# It is now set. Prerequisite: `rclone config` once on the host with a remote
# named "r2". Until that exists the run logs a WARNING and still completes — the
# offsite copy is deliberately non-fatal to the LOCAL backup (see
# scripts/backup.sh), but the run then ends RESULT=DEGRADED with exit 10.
# Check the log after installing:
#   grep -E 'RESULT=|OFFSITE_' /var/log/jago-backup.log | tail
#
# WHY THE COMMAND CHANGED — silent-backup incident, 4-6 Aug 2026
# --------------------------------------------------------------
# The previous line invoked the script BY PATH. scripts/backup.sh is tracked in
# git as mode 100644, so the host checkout was 644 and bash refused it with
# exit 126 — "Permission denied" — every single night, for three nights, while
# cron itself reported nothing wrong. Calling `/bin/bash <script>` makes this
# line immune to a missing executable bit. The git index mode is fixed to
# 100755 in the same change, so the two fixes are independent on purpose.
#
# NO flock HERE, DELIBERATELY. The anti-overlap lock lives inside backup.sh so
# that manual runs are protected too. Wrapping this line in flock as well would
# put two layers on the same lock file, and the inner acquisition would fail
# against the outer one on every run — turning every backup into RESULT=SKIPPED.
#
# Exit codes (see scripts/backup.sh):
#   0 OK · 10 DEGRADED (local ok, offsite unverified) · 75 SKIPPED (lock) · 1 FAIL
#
# RETENTION_DAYS=30 IS A TEMPORARY POLICY, NOT THE TARGET
# -------------------------------------------------------
# The script's own default is 14 days. It is overridden to 30 here for one
# reason: rclone is not installed on this host, so every backup still lives on
# the same disk as the database it protects. While that is true, local history
# depth is the ONLY recovery net there is, and pruning it at 14 days narrows the
# only thing standing between us and total loss.
#
# Do NOT lower this back to 14 until all three are true:
#   1. offsite upload succeeds,
#   2. the uploaded object reads back and its size matches (OFFSITE_OK),
#   3. a restore drill into a disposable database has been approved and passed.
# Until then a run ends RESULT=DEGRADED with exit 10 — that is the correct
# outcome, NOT a failure: the local backup is valid, written and retained; only
# the off-host copy is missing. Reserve exit 1 / RESULT=FAIL for "no usable
# backup exists at all".
#
# Still NO flock on the line below (see the paragraph above): the anti-overlap
# lock lives inside backup.sh so that manual runs are covered too.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

15 2 * * * root COMPOSE_DIR=/var/www/jago-akademi RETENTION_DAYS=30 R2_REMOTE=r2:jago-backups /bin/bash /var/www/jago-akademi/scripts/backup.sh >> /var/log/jago-backup.log 2>&1
